def add(sub,block,title,why,facts,static,analysis,trap,mains,src='PRS',day=0,slug=None,ap=False,p='P1'):
 keys=['E11-'+x for x in src.split(',')] if src else [];extra={}
 if slug:
  art=next(a for a in D['2026-04']['articles'] if a['url'].endswith('/'+slug));k='V'+str(D['2026-04']['articles'].index(art)+1).zfill(2);source(k,'Vision IAS · April2026 · '+art['title'],art['url'],'Public body retrieved; selected lead/substantive passages inspected, not full issue/article or independent review of all underlying references.');keys.append('E11-'+k);extra=dict(magazine_edition='2026-04',magazine_posted='2026-05-22',content_type='magazine-supplement')
 J.append(dict(id=f'E11-2604-{len(J)+1:03}',date='2026-04-'+(f'{day:02}' if day and not slug else '30'),date_precision='day' if day and not slug else 'month',subject=sub,block=block,title=title,why=why+(' April is the editorial coverage index; public web posting was22May. Event/release dates can be earlier.' if slug else ''),facts=facts.split('|'),static_link=static,analysis=analysis.split('|'),trap=trap,mains=mains,priority=p,ap=ap,sources=keys,status='Historical April-indexed snapshot, not certification of current law, latest data or completed implementation',checked='2026-11-07',evidence_access='Registry records actual reading/access scope. Static links, analysis and exam guidance are original.',**extra))
add('Polity & Governance','01 · Parliament and legislative stages','Budget-session closure: extension and scrutiny','The session was adjourned sine die on18April after extra sittings.','The session ran28January–18April2026 and recorded31sittings.|The review reports10introduced and six passed bills in its substantive legislative tally; Budget/appropriation business is separately discussed.|Additional sittings16–18April considered a linked delimitation package; the Constitution amendment was defeated.','Adjournment sine die ends sittings without fixing a further date; prorogation is a distinct presidential act.','The March resumption was not the start of the session; a chronology prevents a false1February commencement date.|Committee referral, House passage and statutory commencement remain separate study fields.','Do not equate adjournment with dissolution or assume every introduced bill passed.','How should legislative output be assessed alongside deliberation and scrutiny?',day=18)
add('Polity & Governance','02 · Delimitation and federal representation','Defeated delimitation package: proposals are not constitutional changes','Three linked bills were introduced16April; the Constitution amendment was negatived.','The proposed131st amendment would raise the maximum LokSabha size from550 to850 and alter census/delimitation provisions.|The package would change the census linkage governing commencement of women’s reservation; it did not itself implement reservation.|After the Constitution bill failed, the dependent Delimitation and UT-law bills were not taken up in the reviewed account.','An Article368 special majority requires a majority of the House’s total membership plus at least two-thirds present and voting; ratification additionally applies where constitutionally required.','Population equality interacts with federal concerns about states that reduced fertility; distinguish equal constituency populations from equal state representation.|Rejection preserves the existing constitutional position; a proposed ceiling is not an actual elected membership.','Do not write that the Constitution now allows850seats or that the rejected bill was the131st enacted amendment.','Evaluate representation, demographic change and federal fairness without treating a defeated bill as law.',day=17)
add('Economy','01 · Inflation release vintage','13April CPI: March provisional versus February final','MoSPI’s13April release uses the2024=100 CPI series.','March2026 provisional combined CPI inflation is3.40%; food inflation is3.87%.|February final combined CPI inflation is3.21%; March’s index level is104.84, not3.40.|PRS separately reports Q4 average CPI inflation3.12%; a quarter average is not the March rate.','An index level, year-on-year rate and quarterly average answer different questions; publication month differs from reference month.','Disaggregated food/rural/urban evidence can explain household experience better than one national rate.|New-base and earlier-series comparisons require consistent baskets, weights and revision labels.','These are not April inflation data; April’s release was scheduled forMay. Provisional values may be revised.','Why should inflation analysis preserve reference period, basket and revision status?',src='CPI,PRS',day=13)
add('Economy','02 · Monetary-policy decisions','April MPC hold and later publication of minutes','The6–8April meeting’s minutes were published22April.','The MPC unanimously retained the repo rate at5.25%.|SDF remained5.00%, with MSF and BankRate5.50%; the stance remained neutral.|The primary minutes identify global supply/energy and financial-market risks alongside domestic resilience.','The policy repo rate is an instrument, not a direct administrative price for every retail loan; minutes explain the earlier decision.','Supply shocks create a growth–inflation trade-off rather than a simple mechanical response to one CPI number.|Neutral preserves flexibility; transmission to lending/deposit rates depends on benchmarks, liquidity and bank decisions.','22April is the minutes date, not a second repo decision. Neutral does not guarantee the next move is a cut.','Discuss monetary-policy choices when external supply shocks affect both growth and inflation.',src='MPC,PRS',day=8)
add('Economy','03 · PPI consultation','Prepaid-payment draft: categories and proposed limits','RBI issued draft PPI Master Directions inApril.','The draft proposes general-purpose and special-purpose categories and a cross-border-use prohibition under its framework.|For full-KYC PPIs, the proposed monthly cash-loading limit is₹10,000, compared with₹50,000 in the reviewed earlier framework.|The draft introduces a₹25,000monthly person-to-person transfer limit for full-KYC PPIs.','A wallet’s stored value differs from a bank deposit account; cash loading, outstanding balance and transfers are different limits.','Tighter controls may reduce misuse but can constrain legitimate cash-dependent users; accessibility and proportionate KYC matter.|A redesign must be assessed against fraud risk, interoperability and merchant/user costs.','A consultation draft is not the operative rulebook;₹10,000is not a universal limit on every UPI or bank-account transaction.','How can wallet regulation balance financial inclusion with risk management?',day=22,p='P2')
add('Economy','04 · Social-impact finance','AIF social-impact entry threshold and investor protection','SEBI’s18April amendment is covered by the review.','PRS reports reduction of the individual minimum for a social-impact fund from₹2lakh to₹1,000.|These funds are linked to eligible not-for-profit securities on the social-stock-exchange framework.|The amendment also provides for identifying an AIF as inoperative; category-specific conditions remain relevant.','Social-impact funds are a specified segment of the AIF framework, not ordinary bank deposits; the parent AIF regulations date to2012.','Lower entry sizes can widen participation, but investors need clear information on instruments, outcomes and risks.|Social purpose does not remove governance, disclosure or verification needs.','₹1,000is not the new minimum for every AIF or a guarantee of commercial returns. PRS’s2016parent-regulation label is not reused.','What safeguards make small-ticket social finance credible?',src='AIF,PRS',day=18,p='P2')
add('Economy','05 · SEZ domestic clearances','Conditional SEZ–DTA concessions: check the denominator','The notified concession framework applies1April2026–31March2027.','Eligible units must have commenced production on/before31March2025 and meet at least20%value addition.|The DTA-sale cap is30%of the highest annual FOB export value in any of the immediately preceding three financial years.|Certification, audit, excluded products/units and prevention of double benefits are part of the design.','SEZ-to-DTA clearance attracts the applicable customs treatment; concessional does not mean blanket duty-free domestic sale.','Capacity utilisation may improve during weak export demand, while the cap preserves export orientation.|A unit needs its own product classification and compliance evidence; not every SEZ activity qualifies.','The cap is not30%of current-year total production, and value addition is not identical to the duty rate.','Assess temporary SEZ flexibility against export incentives and competition in the domestic market.',src='SEZ,PRS',day=1)
add('Economy','06 · Export-risk protection','RELIEF extension: geographic insurance coverage','The April review records expanded export-risk support.','RELIEF was launched19March under the ExportPromotionMission amid war-related trade risks.|April expansion added Egypt and Jordan to reviewed coverage.|Insurance eligibility, covered loss and claim terms remain distinct from shipment value and general export incentives.','Export credit/risk insurance transfers specified risks; it does not prevent disruption or guarantee payment for every commercial loss.','Risk support can keep viable trade moving, but exporters still need route, buyer and contract due diligence.|Geographic coverage should not be confused with a tariff preference or unrestricted sovereign guarantee.','Expansion does not mean every shipment’s entire value is automatically reimbursed.','How can trade-risk support complement, rather than replace, exporter risk management?',day=17,p='P2')
add('International Relations','01 · New Zealand treaty stages','India–New Zealand FTA: signing is not entry into force','The primary PIB release records signing on27April.','The announced agreement offers NewZealand duty-free access for100%of India’s exports, subject to treaty operation and rules.|India’s offer covers about70%of tariff lines, not an identical reciprocal100%; sensitive products remain excluded.|Services access, temporary professional mobility and a US$20billion investment commitment over15years are reported design elements.','Negotiation conclusion, signature, domestic procedures and entry into force are different treaty stages; tariff lines and trade-value coverage differ.','Labour-intensive exports may gain, but origin rules, standards and delivery capacity determine actual utilisation.|For AP, examine eligible seafood/food-processing market access and standards without assuming all agricultural products receive symmetrical Indian concessions.','Do not certify current zero duties from signing alone, call the commitment completed investment, or use28April as the signing date.','How should India translate an FTA’s market access into practical export capability?',src='NZ,PRS',day=27)
add('Science & Technology','01 · Online-game regulation','Gaming Rules: notification inApril, commencement inMay','The reviewed rules were notified22April; the inspected legal summary identifies1May commencement.','The framework distinguishes online money games, e-sports and other online games under the parent2025Act.|Determination examines fees/stakes, expectations of gains and monetisation of rewards/assets.|PRS describes registration for e-sports or notified categories and ten-year registration validity, not a requirement that every casual game register identically.','Rule notification and legal commencement can occur on different dates; a game’s label does not conclusively determine its legal category.','Classification needs predictable criteria and appeal/redress, while payment controls and child protection require practical coordination.|Gaming policy also intersects with data protection and consumer transparency.','Do not present the rules as operative on22April merely because published then, or equate all online games with prohibited money games.','How can game classification protect users without indiscriminate prohibition?',src='PRS,GAMING',day=22)
add('Environment','01 · Underground coal gasification','UCG mining plans: energy extraction and groundwater risk','Coal-ministry guidelines were released6April.','Coal/lignite blocks proposed for underground gasification require a mining plan approved by the CoalControllerOrganisation before operations.|The reviewed safety design includes subsidence/fire/groundwater controls and at least500metres between coexisting mining and gasification operations.|Closure includes well sealing, cavity stabilisation and three-year post-closure groundwater monitoring in the reviewed guidelines.','Underground gasification converts coal in situ into usable gas; it differs from physically excavating coal for surface combustion.','Access to otherwise difficult resources must be weighed against hydrogeological uncertainty and monitoring capacity.|Escrow-backed closure obligations help address liabilities that outlast production.','An approved mining plan is not proof of zero contamination or exemption from all other permissions.','Evaluate UCG through energy security, environmental risk and enforceable closure planning.',day=6)
add('Economy','07 · Garment-export remission','RoSCTL extension: embedded taxes, not all export costs','The textile-export rebate scheme was extended inApril.','The reviewed extension runs up to30September2026 or earlier approval for the16thFinanceCommission period.|RoSCTL covers eligible apparel and made-ups under its prescribed framework.|It rebates embedded central/state taxes not otherwise reimbursed rather than duplicate refunds.','RoSCTL and RoDTEP are distinct remission arrangements; product coverage and notified schedules matter.','Tax neutrality can support MSME competitiveness but cannot alone offset logistics, energy or market-demand shocks.|Monitor actual claim access and payment delays rather than equate scheme extension with increased export orders.','Do not call this a uniform subsidy on every textile item or an unconditional extension beyond the stated endpoint.','Assess remission schemes as part of a broader textile-export strategy.',day=1,p='P2')
add('Society & Welfare','01 · Rural connectivity','PMGSY-III: different deadlines for hill bridges','Cabinet continued PMGSY-III on18April with revised outlay.','The revised outlay is₹83,977crore, up from₹80,250crore.|Roads/bridges in plains and roads in hills have aMarch2028deadline; hill bridges extend toMarch2029.|The scheme consolidates through routes and major rural links to markets, higher-secondary schools and hospitals.','Road connectivity is a service network: construction, maintenance, all-weather reliability and access to destinations all matter.','Tendering eligible older sanctioned works can address backlog, but execution quality and lifecycle maintenance remain essential.|For AP, use travel-time, seasonal access and service-use outcomes rather than assume every village gets a newly sanctioned road.','March2028is not the deadline for every hill bridge, and revised outlay is not spending already incurred.','How should rural-road programmes be evaluated beyond kilometres constructed?',src='PMGSY,PRS',day=18)
add('Economy','08 · Highway fees and loading','Overload fee tiers are not permission to overload','April amendments revise national-highway fee treatment of overloaded vehicles.','The reviewed fee tiers are no overload fee up to10%excess, twice the base fee above10%through40%, and four times above40%.|Certified weighing facilities underpin assessment.|PRS reports no overload fee if the fee plaza lacks the prescribed weighing facility.','A toll-fee rule and vehicle weight/safety law regulate different legal questions.','Calibrated fees may reduce arbitrary charging, but enforcement must not make dangerous loading commercially attractive.|Reliable measurement, receipts and grievance handling are necessary for fair administration.','No additional overload fee is not a legal exemption from every permissible-weight or road-safety requirement.','How can freight enforcement protect roads and safety without arbitrary penalties?',day=13,p='P2')
add('Environment','02 · Coastal oil pollution — draft','Tar-ball management: proposed lifecycle responsibility','MoEFCC released draft rules3April for consultation.','Tar balls are weathered oil residues; potential sources include spills, leakages and natural seepage.|The draft covers collection, storage, transport, treatment and disposal, with proposed SPCB authorisation.|It assigns district/state/pollution-board roles and proposes response capacity and environmental compensation.','Weathering can change oil’s form without making it ecologically harmless; source attribution needs evidence.','For AP’s coast, planning should link shoreline reporting, trained collection, worker protection and authorised waste handling.|Preparedness benefits fisheries and tourism, but declaring responsibility does not establish that a specific operator caused every incident.','The draft does not itself prove final statewide duties are in force. Do not infer blanket environmental-clearance exemptions from a secondary summary.','Design a coastal oil-residue response that connects pollution control with local livelihoods.',day=3)
add('International Relations','02 · Austria and sector cooperation','Austria visit: agreements, intent and implementation','The Chancellor’s14–17April visit produced a reviewed outcomes list.','Cooperation covered film/audio-visual work, food safety, roads and a space-industry seminar.|Letters of intent addressed military cooperation, counter-terrorism and vocational training.|Investment facilitation, startup links and cyber/education dialogue featured among announcements.','An MoU, a letter of intent and an implemented project need not create identical legal obligations.','Skills and industrial cooperation can be valuable where institutions convert intent into training places or research outputs.|Evaluate milestones and counterpart institutions instead of counting all announcements as completed investment.','Do not equate the visit with an FTA or assume every MoU guarantees a funded project.','What makes sectoral diplomacy translate into measurable cooperation?',day=16,p='P2')
add('International Relations','03 · Republic of Korea','Korea visit: CEPA-upgrade talks and wider partnerships','The19–21April state visit produced agreements and announced initiatives.','The review records15MoUs across ports, industry, trade, science and culture.|The parties declared resumption of negotiations to upgrade their existing CEPA.|Maritime/climate cooperation and participation in wider initiatives were among the announced outcomes.','Upgrading an existing agreement differs from concluding a replacement treaty or commencing a new tariff schedule.','Industrial and maritime cooperation can deepen supply chains, but local capability, standards and execution determine gains.|Separate announced intent to join an institution from verified completed accession.','Do not label resumed CEPA talks a completed upgraded FTA or treat every announced institutional intention as final membership.','Assess the economic and maritime dimensions of India–Korea engagement.',day=20,p='P2')
add('Economy','09 · Insolvency reform','IBC2026: assent and provision-specific commencement','The Gazette records Presidential assent on6April.','The amendment’s opening section allows different notified commencement dates for different provisions.|The reviewed reform includes creditor-initiated resolution and enabling group/cross-border frameworks; details require the applicable text/rules.|The primary opening clarifies agreement-based security interest and requires written reasons for specified admission delays.','Resolving a viable debtor, selling assets and liquidating a company are different outcomes; creditor recovery needs a stated denominator.','Faster processes can preserve going-concern value, but tribunal capacity and fair treatment of stakeholder classes still matter.|An enabling framework is not proof every new procedure was usable immediately on assent.','Do not backdate later commencement to6April or copy recovery percentages without distinguishing admitted claims from liquidation value.','How can insolvency reform improve speed while retaining fairness and value preservation?',src='IBC',slug='insolvency-and-bankruptcy-code-amendment-act-2026')
add('Society & Welfare','02 · Platform work and protections','Gig-work welfare: a neighbouring-state comparison, not AP law','April’s magazine examines Telangana’s platform-worker legislation and broader gig-work issues.','Platform work can sit outside the conventional employer–employee relationship while still involving substantial economic dependence.|The article describes registration, a welfare board/fund and grievance/algorithmic-transparency mechanisms in Telangana’s framework.|National SocialSecurityCode financing and a state transaction-based levy are different designs; neither should be silently attributed to AP.','Worker status, social-security entitlement and actual benefit delivery are separate questions.','Portable benefits can support multi-platform workers, but registration, contribution collection and grievance access determine reach.|For AP answers, evaluate possible lessons without inventing a newly enacted equivalent state statute.','The selected state-Act account is secondary evidence; commencement/levy notifications were not independently read. Forecast worker totals are not observed employment.','Design portable protection for platform workers while preserving flexible work opportunities.',src='',slug='gig-economy-2')
add('Economy','10 · Labour statistics — dated carry-forward','Annual PLFS2025: March release inApril’s magazine','The primary release is27March and measures January–December2025; April is a revision index.','For age15+in usual status, LFPR is59.3%, WPR57.4%and UR3.1%.|Male/female LFPR are79.1%and40.0%; regular wage/salaried work accounts for23.6%of workers.|Youth15–29usual-status unemployment is9.9%; it is not interchangeable with the all-age15+rate.','LFPR uses population as denominator, while unemployment uses the labour force; usual status and current-weekly status differ.','Low unemployment can coexist with low participation, insecure work and low earnings; employment quality needs separate evidence.|The primary describes gender gaps in hours worked; it does not label the quoted male–female differences as unpaid-work hours.','Do not call this April’s monthly survey, mix status/age groups or treat nominal wage growth as real wage growth.','Explain why headline unemployment alone is an incomplete labour-market diagnosis.',src='PLFS',slug='periodic-labour-force-survey-plfs-annual-report-2025')
add('Agriculture','01 · Oilseed value chains','Edible-oil self-reliance: production, processing and incentives','The April issue revisits theMarch parliamentary report on oilseeds and pulses.','The article cites approximately56%import dependence and15.66MMTimports for2023–24; these are dated secondary report figures.|Rainfed production, yield variability, seed systems and processing affect domestic supply.|Expanded procurement and trade measures discussed in the report are recommendations, not automatic universal purchases.','Oilseed output and edible-oil availability differ because oil recovery, processing and consumption patterns matter.','For AP, compare agronomic suitability, water demand, mill access and farmer returns before expanding a particular crop.|Import protection may help growers but can raise consumer costs; predictable policy and productivity improvements must work together.','Do not equate an import-share estimate for2023–24 with April2026’s final balance or presume every GM/seed claim in commentary is established evidence.','How can edible-oil self-reliance reconcile farmer incomes, water use and consumer affordability?',src='',slug='self-sufficiency-in-edible-oils')
add('Economy','11 · Industrial incentives','PLI: incremental sales versus domestic value addition','April’s magazine reviews PLI performance, including food processing.','The PLI umbrella covers14sectors with a stated₹1.97lakhcrore outlay.|Incentives generally link to eligible incremental production/sales under sector-specific conditions.|Investment committed, realised investment, approved claims and actual incentive payments measure different stages.','Gross output, assembly activity and domestic value added are not identical indicators of industrial capability.','Supplier development and technology learning determine whether scale persists after incentives decline.|For AP food-processing opportunities, assess raw-material supply, cold chains and market demand rather than assume all firms qualify.','An aggregate success claim does not establish equal performance across all14sectors or completed payment of the total outlay.','How should PLI be evaluated for additionality and durable domestic capability?',src='',slug='production-linked-incentive-pli-scheme')
add('Security','01 · Road safety and institutions','Phalodi-linked road-safety directions: legal claims need the order','The magazine discusses SupremeCourt directions following the Phalodi accident.','Its account links safe commuting with Article21and describes highway surveillance, emergency response and district coordination.|The article reports road-side encroachment and heavy-vehicle management measures.|The actual order was not independently read here; detailed deadlines/distances remain attributed secondary claims, not certified legal instructions.','The safe-system approach combines safe roads, vehicles, speeds, users and post-crash care.','Effective enforcement requires accountable agencies and working emergency services, not only cameras.|For AP, connect highway engineering, trauma referral and district coordination without assuming every reported facility is installed.','Do not generalise a summary into an unchecked universal ban on every roadside business or claim compliance with the Court’s full order.','How can an integrated safe-system approach reduce road deaths more effectively than fines alone?',src='',slug='road-safety-in-india')
add('Society & Welfare','03 · Wages and industrial relations','Worker protests: formal rules and lived insecurity','April’s magazine discusses protests in several industrial hubs.','Contracting chains, wage pressure, working conditions and weak grievance channels feature in the account.|The four labour codes consolidate a legal framework, but provision-specific operation and state rules need separate checks.|The central floor wage and minimum wages set by appropriate governments are distinct legal concepts.','A statutory protection is not the same as effective coverage, payment or accessible enforcement.','Transparent payslips, credible worker representation and timely wage-dispute resolution can reduce avoidable conflict.|AP applications should examine industrial compliance and welfare delivery rather than import another state’s local protest facts.','Do not invent two identical nationally fixed wage rates from the magazine’s wording or assume registration alone delivers social security.','How can labour reform combine industrial competitiveness with credible worker protections?',src='',slug='workers-protests')
add('Agriculture','02 · Resilient production systems','Record foodgrain output is not proof of resilient livelihoods','The issue uses reported2024–25production to examine agricultural resilience.','The article cites357.73MMTfoodgrain output for2024–25; it is a dated source figure, not April2026’s harvest outcome.|Resilience requires input efficiency, diverse production, risk protection, storage and markets.|Output, farm income and nutritional diversity should be assessed separately.','A national production record can coexist with local crop losses and financially vulnerable smallholders.','For AP, connect climate-resilient varieties, water budgeting, extension and FPO/market access.|Stability depends on institutions that absorb weather and price shocks rather than only increasing aggregate tonnage.','Do not conclude every farmer benefited equally or use a secondary production estimate as an undated current final statistic.','What makes a production system resilient rather than merely high-yielding?',src='',slug='indias-resilient-production-systems-in-agriculture')
add('Economy','12 · Payments strategy','PaymentsVision2028: roadmap is not an immediate liability rule','April’s magazine discusses RBI’s payments roadmap and UPI’s first decade.','The roadmap includes user controls, fraud-risk response, wider oversight and cross-border authorisation simplification.|TReDS interoperability concerns receivables-finance platforms, not a universal cancellation of trade credit.|Proposed shared fraud responsibility needs applicable directions before being treated as a settled entitlement.','A vision document sets priorities; binding implementation arises through the relevant laws, directions and systems.','Interoperability can reduce switching frictions, while resilience needs competition, security and accessible redress.|A user switch-off facility must be usable in practice without excluding people who need assisted access.','Do not claim every roadmap feature is already universally available or every loss is automatically jointly reimbursed.','How should a payments roadmap balance scale, competition and consumer trust?',src='',slug='payments-vision-2028')
add('Economy','13 · Fraud safeguards — discussion','Cooling-off proposals: fraud prevention versus payment speed','The magazine covers RBI’s discussion of additional digital-fraud safeguards.','Ideas include a one-hour delay for specified transfers above₹10,000, with proposed trusted/whitelisted exceptions.|Other options include user-controlled limits, extra safeguards for vulnerable users and scrutiny of mule accounts.|An authorised push-payment fraud can involve a deceived user authenticating the transaction.','Authentication verifies an action/credential; it does not prove that consent was free from deception.','A delay may enable cancellation but can impede genuine time-sensitive transfers; design should use evidence and calibrated exceptions.|Trusted-person safeguards must preserve autonomy and not become an automatic barrier for all older or disabled users.','These are discussion-paper options, not a universal current one-hour delay on every UPI transfer.','Evaluate proportionate anti-fraud friction in an instant-payments system.',src='',slug='digital-payment-frauds')
add('Science & Technology','02 · AI and internal security','AI-assisted policing: assistance is not a substitute for proof','The article carries forward theMarch30parliamentary AI-impact report.','Discussed uses include entity resolution, multilingual assistance, crime-pattern analysis and fraud detection.|CCTNS-related upgrades and agency applications are described at different deployment stages.|Predictive outputs need validation and lawful human decision-making; a risk score is not proof of guilt.','Article21due process, privacy and non-arbitrariness apply to technology-assisted state action.','Biased or incomplete records can amplify profiling; independent audits and correction mechanisms are necessary.|For AP, assess access controls, accuracy and accountability before assuming a tool’s national mention proves local deployment.','Do not turn a proposed capability into universally operational surveillance or treat algorithmic prediction as admissible proof by itself.','What safeguards should govern AI in public-security decision-making?',src='',slug='emergence-of-ai-in-indias-internal-security-architecture')
add('Security','02 · Defence-industry evidence','Defence exports: annual values and domestic capability','The2April primary announcement reports FY2025–26exports.','Exports reached₹38,424crore versus₹23,622crore inFY2024–25, a62.66%increase.|DPSUs contributed₹21,071crore and private firms₹17,353crore, approximately54.84%and45.16%.|The primary states exports to more than80countries; the magazine’s broader undated100-plus claim is not used as the same fiscal snapshot.','Defence exports, total defence production and indigenous content are different measures.','Sustained competitiveness depends on technology, reliability, export authorisation and lifecycle support.|Record gross export value does not prove independence from imported components or equal growth in all firms.','Do not add production/export totals as identical categories or present a draft procurement procedure as already operative.','Assess export growth alongside technological depth and responsible defence trade.',src='DEF',slug='indias-defence-exports-2')
add('Environment','03 · Renewable-energy measurement','Renewables: capacity rankings do not establish generation share','The issue reviews renewable-capacity and electricity-transition reports.','Installed capacity measures rated potential; generation measures actual electricity over time.|Non-fossil capacity includes nuclear, while renewable capacity is a narrower category.|The article’s51.5%demand statement is not adopted as a verified generation statistic; its capacity/generation measures are inconsistent.','GWmeasures power capacity; GWh/TWhor billion units measure energy produced over a period.','Grid integration, storage and flexible resources determine how capacity additions translate into reliable supply.|AP policy should evaluate evacuation, curtailment, land and distribution finances, not only project announcements.','Do not call a capacity ranking the same thing as global renewable electricity production rank or equate51.5%capacity with energy demand met.','How should clean-energy progress be measured beyond installed gigawatts?',src='',slug='renewable-energy-in-india')
add('Environment','04 · Water systems and irreversible loss','Water bankruptcy: a diagnostic metaphor, not a court status','The magazine discusses UNU-INWEH’s water-bankruptcy framework.','The concept concerns long-run use beyond renewable inflows and safe depletion limits, with lasting damage.|It distinguishes an acute water crisis from persistent depletion and effectively irreversible loss.|Surface flows, groundwater, wetlands and glaciers have different storage/replenishment dynamics.','A water balance compares inflows, withdrawals and storage changes; economic extraction limits differ from sustainable ecological limits.','For AP, basin-wide groundwater budgeting should connect irrigation, urban demand and ecosystem needs.|Demand reform and crop choice can be more durable than supplying a new source to sustain unsustainable use.','This is an analytical framework, not a formal declaration that every aquifer or all water everywhere is physically exhausted.','How can water governance respond when overuse has eroded natural buffers?',src='',slug='water-bankruptcy-1')
add('Science & Technology','03 · Crewed lunar exploration','ArtemisII: completed flyby, not a lunar landing','NASA’s recap records1April launch and10April return.','ArtemisIIwas the first crewed Orion flight, lasting nearly10days around the Moon.|The crew comprised ReidWiseman, VictorGlover, ChristinaKoch and Canada’s JeremyHansen.|The crew splashed down in the Pacific near SanDiego; testing crewed deep-space systems differs from landing on the lunar surface.','A flyby trajectory, lunar orbit and a surface landing are different mission profiles.','Mission success supplies evidence for particular crew/spacecraft operations; it does not guarantee all later lunar systems are ready.|Compare mission objectives before judging different national programmes by a single distance or crew record.','Do not write that ArtemisIIlanded astronauts on the Moon or that itsApril completion means a permanent lunar base exists.','How do incremental test missions reduce risk in human spaceflight?',src='NASA',slug='artemis-ii-moon-mission')
add('Society & Welfare','04 · OneHealth coordination','OneHealth: linking human, animal and ecosystem health','The April issue discusses a OneHealth summit in Lyon.','OneHealth integrates human, animal, plant and environmental health rather than treating zoonoses solely as hospital problems.|The Quadripartite partners are WHO, FAO, UNEP and WOAH.|The article describes strengthened scientific advice, practical networks and attention to rabies and avian influenza.','Surveillance, prevention and response must connect veterinary, public-health and environmental information.','For AP, livestock/poultry surveillance, laboratories and risk communication should share actionable protocols.|Data sharing needs clear responsibilities and capacity; a summit announcement is not proof of district-level integrated response.','OneHealth is not the merger of all agencies into WHO or a promise that every zoonosis can be eliminated by one intervention.','Design an implementable OneHealth response to zoonotic risk.',src='',slug='one-health-approach-1')
add('Culture & History','01 · Social reform and anniversaries','JyotibaPhule:199years, education and social equality','The11April1827birth date makes April2026the199thanniversary.','The200thbirth anniversary falls in2027; a bicentenary-year programme beginning in2026is a different description.|Jyotiba and SavitribaiPhule worked for girls’ education and anti-caste social reform.|SatyashodhakSamaj was founded in1873; Gulamgiri also dates to1873.','Education can challenge inherited social exclusion; reform movements and later constitutional safeguards belong to different historical periods.','Link educational access with dignity, gender equality and peasant concerns, rather than reduce the movement to one school’s date.|For APPSC comparison, examine social-reform strategies without conflating different regional movements.','Do not repeat the magazine’s “this year200thanniversary” as completed arithmetic or attribute all work solely to Jyotiba without Savitribai’s role.','How did educational reform become a strategy for social emancipation?',src='',slug='mahatma-jyotiba-phule',p='P2')
add('Polity & Governance','03 · Proportionate compliance','JanVishwas: trust requires credible enforcement','April’s issue reviews the2026legislative reform.','The primary revised scope is79CentralActs and784provisions, including717decriminalisation and67ease-of-living amendments.|Graded warnings, civil penalties and adjudication seek more proportionate treatment of specified lapses.|The March volume’s earlier80Actcount is corrected from the primary27March introduction release.','Decriminalisation does not abolish the regulatory duty; an administrative penalty still needs lawful procedure and review.','Credible trust combines easier compliance with predictable detection and proportionate enforcement.|Small businesses need understandable obligations and accessible appeals, not merely lower formal penalties.','Do not describe all offences as abolished or count Acts, provisions and offences as interchangeable. Detailed commencement remains separately unchecked.','What makes trust-based regulation effective rather than permissive?',src='JAN,JANAPR',slug='trust-based-governance')
add('Polity & Governance','04 · Census phases and safeguards','Census2027: April rollout is not completed population enumeration','The first-phase programme is discussed inApril’s magazine.','The exercise is governed by the CensusAct1948and CensusRules1990 under the Union framework.|Houselisting/housing data and population enumeration are separate phases, with state-specific schedules.|Digital capture and optional self-enumeration supplement field verification; they do not mean only smartphone owners are counted.','Census confidentiality, complete coverage and comparable definitions are essential to a statistical baseline.','AP’s schedule must be read separately from the national operating window.|Caste enumeration plans must distinguish comprehensive enumeration from SC/STinformation collected in past censuses.','Do not say every state began household visits on1April, that the census is complete, or that no caste-related data were collected after1931.','How can a digital census improve coverage while protecting confidentiality and inclusion?',src='',slug='census-2027-3')
add('Culture & History','02 · Amaravati heritage','Amaravati heritage is not the same geographic object as the capital region','April’s capital legislation provides a linkage to Buddhist heritage.','Amaravati’s Mahachaitya is associated with Buddhist narrative sculpture and the Satavahana-era artistic tradition.|The inspected ASI extract describes locally available light-green limestone, not blanket white-marble construction.|Jataka/Buddha-life scenes, circumambulation and surviving fragments support art-history study; the statutory capital area has its own definition.','A stupa’s drum, anda, harmika, chhatra and pradakshinapatha have distinct structural/ritual functions.','Heritage planning should protect archaeological context while supporting interpretation and local livelihoods.|Distinguish the ancient settlement/monument and modern APCRDA-notified capital geography; avoid stale district labels.','Do not say the modern capital’s full boundary is identical to the ancient stupa site or that nothing survives because the full dome is lost.','How can capital-region growth accommodate archaeological conservation?',src='ASI',slug='amaravati',ap=True,p='P2')
add('Society & Welfare','05 · Rural housing','PMAY-G: sanctioned houses, assistance and service convergence','The April issue revisits the rural housing programme introduced in2016.','The reviewed target combines the earlier2.95crorehouses with another2crore throughFY2028–29.|Standard unit assistance is₹1.20lakh in plains and₹1.30lakh in specified hill/difficult areas, with applicable conditions.|Beneficiary identification, GramSabha verification, geotagging and convergence for amenities are distinct delivery steps.','A pucca structure is not automatically adequate housing without water, sanitation, energy, tenure security and accessibility.','For AP, assess exclusions, instalment timeliness, local construction cost and actual occupancy.|Construction sanctions and completed houses should not be counted as the same outcome.','Do not conflate PMAY-G with the urban scheme or treat4.95croreas houses already completed. The article’s incorrect1996start for IndiraAwasYojana is not reused.','What makes rural housing support translate into dignified habitation?',src='',slug='pradhan-mantri-awaas-yojana-grameen-pmay-g')
add('Society & Welfare','06 · Household vulnerability','Middle-class vulnerability: define the group before quoting rates','April’s article links employment, prices and household security.','There is no single universally interchangeable income-based definition of India’s middle class.|Income volatility, healthcare/education costs and debt service can affect resilience even above poverty thresholds.|The article’s headline graduate-unemployment and double-digit cost claims are not adopted as current official statistics without matching period/cohort evidence.','Nominal income growth, real disposable income and household wealth measure different dimensions.','Use PLFSage/status definitions and the actual CPIrelease rather than combine incompatible estimates for an alarming headline.|Policy can support public services, insurance and productive work without assuming all households face identical inflation.','Do not substitute an older subgroup unemployment rate for the2025PLFSheadline or claim national health/education CPIis automatically double-digit.','How can policy address household insecurity beyond a binary poor/non-poor classification?',src='PLFS,CPI',slug='rise-in-middle-class-vulnerability',p='P2')
add('Polity & Governance','05 · Ethics and business responsibility','Conscious capitalism: purpose needs verifiable conduct','The issue’s ethics essay contrasts narrow profit metrics with stakeholder responsibility.','The approach emphasises purpose, stakeholder value and long-term responsibility alongside financial viability.|Gandhian trusteeship offers a normative connection, not a substitute for enforceable law.|Employees, consumers, communities and ecosystems can bear costs not captured in short-term accounts.','Legal compliance is a minimum; ethical responsibility also asks who bears harm and whether affected people can challenge decisions.','Test purpose statements through wages, safety, supply-chain practice, grievance systems and environmental outcomes.|Counterpoint: vague stakeholder promises can mask concentrated discretion unless board accountability and measurable commitments exist.','A CSRbudget or ethical slogan alone does not prove a firm meets stakeholder obligations.','Develop an ethical assessment of a profitable firm whose contractors expose workers to avoidable harm.',src='',slug='conscious-capitalism',p='P2')
add('Andhra Pradesh','01 · Capital statute and chronology','Amaravati Act: assent6April, deemed effect2June2024','The full Gazette text advances theMarch resolution to enacted legislation.','Act7of2026received assent on6April; LokSabha passed1April and RajyaSabha2April in the inspected PRStrack.|Section5(2)now names Amaravati as the new capital.|The Act deems commencement from2June2024and includes capital-city areas notified under APCRDAAct2014 in its explanation.','Retrospective statutory effect differs from the date of assent, House passage and physical project completion.','Central statutory recognition can reduce administrative uncertainty but does not itself finance or finish capital works.|Link land pooling, service delivery, public finance and heritage safeguards to implementation rather than assume legal naming settles every policy issue.','Do not say theMarchAssembly resolution itself amended the central Act or that no future Parliament can amend the law again.','Explain the significance and limits of statutory recognition for AP’s capital development.',src='APACT',day=6,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','02 · State inflation evidence','AP March inflation in the13April national release','MoSPI’s state table includes AP’s provisionalMarch2026rates.','APcombined CPIinflation is4.05%, compared with national3.40%.|APfood inflation is5.45%, compared with national3.87%.|The table’s highlighted-state universe is states over50lakhpopulation by2011Census; this is not a survey of every household’s actual price increase.','State indices are aggregates; district/item estimates can have thinner samples and different expenditure patterns.','The food headline suggests distributional pressure but cannot establish which commodity caused AP’s entire gap without detailed weights/data.|Use targeted market/supply responses and household evidence rather than infer one universal cost increase.','These areMarchprovisionaldata released inApril, not Aprilprices or a guarantee of later final values.','How should APuse state inflation evidence without overinterpreting aggregate comparisons?',src='CPI',day=13,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','03 · Census field schedule','APcensus: self-enumeration and later field validation','The15Aprilreport gives AP’s first-phase schedule.','Optional self-enumeration runs16–30April2026.|Houselisting/housing-census field visits are scheduled1–30May.|Successful self-enumeration creates an SEIDfor enumerator validation; the reported phase uses33questions on housing/amenities/assets.','Self-entry is an additional collection route, not exemption from verification or a completed population count.','Telugu access and assisted field enumeration can reduce exclusion; privacy and secure handling must accompany participation.|Maintain a state-specific schedule rather than copy a national date into every APdistrict note.','Do not call16Aprilthe start of all door-to-door APvisits or say every household must own a smartphone.','How can APcombine digital convenience with complete census coverage?',src='APCENSUS',day=16,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','04 · Heat risk and public health','APheatwave alerts: forecast versus observation','The15Aprilreport attributes warnings and readings to APSDMA.','Severe conditions were forecast for46mandals and heatwave conditions for73mandals in that dated alert.|The report gives previous-day Ontimitta temperature45°C; a reading and a forecast are different evidence.|Heat exposure varies with humidity, work, housing, hydration and health; temperature alone does not measure every person’s risk.','Heatwave meteorological thresholds and physiological heat stress are related but distinct concepts.','Prioritise outdoor workers, older people and vulnerable settlements through shade, water, rest and accessible care.|Forecast-led action should coordinate APSDMA, local bodies, schools, employers and health facilities; monitor response and heat illness, not only advisories.','Do not turn a forecast count into confirmed outcomes or give the historical alert as today’s weather advice.','Design a locally accountable heat-action response for APdistricts.',src='APHEAT',day=15,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','05 · Polavaram rehabilitation','Polavaram OTS: revised housing and site assistance','The30AprilCabinet decision is reported inTheHindu.','Reported house-construction assistance rises from₹2.85lakh to₹3.57lakh.|For eligible beneficiaries choosing outside-colony construction, reported house-site value rises from₹1lakh to₹2lakh.|These are Cabinet-approved components under the OTSarrangement, not proof every displaced family has been paid.','Rehabilitation includes housing, livelihood restoration, social infrastructure and applicable rights, not cash alone.','Different options require informed choice, clear eligibility and accessible grievance mechanisms.|For displaced tribal and other households, assess actual relocation conditions and access to land/services rather than only a unit-cost increase.','Do not describe these amounts as universal compensation for every loss or as proof all rehabilitation obligations are fulfilled.','What makes rehabilitation adequate beyond a higher cash assistance figure?',src='APCAB',day=30,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','06 · Defence-manufacturing land','Puttaparthi DRDOallotment: land approval is not production','The30AprilCabinet report includes a350-acre allotment.','The report identifies350acres atPuttaparthi for a defence-manufacturing unit underDRDO.|The decision concerns land allocation, not a certified commissioned factory.|Project design, environmental/other permissions, financing and construction milestones require separate records.','Defence R&D, manufacturing capacity and actual production are different parts of a capability chain.','Local benefits depend on skills, supplier linkages and execution rather than acreage alone.|Track employment and procurement claims against actual project documents; do not invent a weapon system or production deadline.','Do not call the allotment proof APalready manufactures a specified system or earns a fixed defence-export share.','How can APturn strategic industrial land allocations into durable local capability?',src='APCAB',day=30,ap=True,p='P2')
add('Andhra Pradesh','07 · Fishing-harbour infrastructure','Three fishing harbours: revised approval and livelihood outcomes','The30Aprilreport records revised coastal-infrastructure approval.','The reported revised approval is₹1,586.69crore forBudagatlapalem, Pudimadaka andKothapatnam.|The report estimates benefits for over12,700fishers and support for more than2,500vessels.|Expected beneficiaries are projections, not evidence that all facilities are complete or outcomes realised.','A fishing harbour links landing, auctioning, ice/cold chain, sanitation, navigation and environmental management.','Safer landings and reduced post-harvest losses depend on effective operations and fair market access.|Assess coastal impacts, waste treatment, maintenance and small-fisher inclusion rather than only harbour construction costs.','Revised approval is not a completed-spending figure, and potential beneficiaries must not be presented as verified realised gains.','How should APmeasure fishing-infrastructure success through livelihoods and ecology?',src='APCAB',day=30,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','08 · Canal modernisation','Punganur branch canal: revised estimate versus delivered water','The30AprilCabinet report concerns HNSSPhase-IIworks.','The reported revised estimate is₹309.92crore for modernising thePunganurbranchcanal.|The report places thesePhase-IIHandri-NeevaSujalaSravanthiworks inSriSathyaSaidistrict.|A financial approval is distinct from a work award, physical completion and actual reliable delivery to farms.','Conveyance capacity, source-water availability, pumping energy and on-farm use jointly determine irrigation service.','Appraise revised costs with engineering need, procurement readiness and long-term O&Mfinance.|Measure seasonal delivery, tail-end access and water productivity rather than assume canal works automatically solve basin scarcity.','Do not claim₹309.92croreis already spent or infer newly irrigated acreage without a dated project record.','How can APcombine irrigation modernisation with transparent costs and water-use efficiency?',src='APCAB',day=30,ap=True)
